A team is building a design system for a web application. They have defined the following color tokens:

```
--color-blue-100: #EBF8FF;
--color-blue-500: #3B82F6;
--color-blue-700: #1D4ED8;
--color-red-500: #EF4444;
--color-green-500: #22C55E;
--color-gray-100: #F3F4F6;
--color-gray-900: #111827;
```

These are used directly in components:
```css
.button-primary { background-color: var(--color-blue-500); }
.button-danger { background-color: var(--color-red-500); }
.badge-success { background-color: var(--color-green-500); }
.surface-default { background-color: var(--color-gray-100); }
```

The team wants to add dark mode support next quarter.

A design system team is proposing a Button component API:

```typescript
interface ButtonProps {
  label: string;
  color: 'blue' | 'red' | 'gray' | 'green';
  size: 'small' | 'medium' | 'large';
  fontWeight: 'normal' | 'medium' | 'bold';
  paddingLeft: number;
  paddingRight: number;
  borderRadius: number;
  onClick: () => void;
  disabled?: boolean;
}
```

The API was designed by asking "what visual properties might callers need to customize?"

A team has 200 files using a legacy typography system with direct values:
```css
/* Legacy — used in 200 files */
.title { font-size: 24px; font-weight: 700; }
.subtitle { font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600; }
.body-text { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; }
.caption { font-size: 12px; font-weight: 400; }
```

The new design system defines a token-based type scale:
```css
--text-2xl: 24px; --text-xl: 18px; --text-base: 14px; --text-sm: 12px;
--font-bold: 700; --font-semibold: 600; --font-normal: 400;
```

The migration plan is: delete all legacy classes this sprint, update all 200 files in parallel.
